 delivery documents
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sixth upload (NovaAPI-v14, 24dc3e6) arrived at the git root for the first
time in six deliveries: tools/check_layout.sh passed on the fresh clone, and
GitHub ran the `backend` workflow on the push with 3/3 jobs green
(run 43252213875). No migration was needed.

Everything was re-verified in a clean environment (new clone, new virtualenv,
same library versions as the previous pass):

  10/10 gates · 451 tests · 94% coverage · 15/15 missions · 93 actions /
  0 mistakes · readiness 100 (S) · 67/67 operations audited for player text
  in-process and over a real socket · 12 offline + 14 live probes · 0 failures
  (NASA POWER live) · preview smoke test against the running server.

Three unfinished items are closed:

* releases/SHA256SUMS.txt described a patch and a zip that were not in the
  tree; both are regenerated from the committed tree above 24dc3e6.
* The delivery documents still named the retired AbdElrhmanAhmed7/Final and
  baseline 11cefe5. Current pointers now name NovaAPI-v14 / 24dc3e6
  (PROJECT_STATUS.md §9.7 + §13, MIGRATION.md §10, releases/README.md,
  verification/README.md). Earlier sections are kept unchanged as history.
* The CI path filters covered only NOVA/backend/** and the workflow file, yet
  pytest gates the root documents (test_project_docs.py) and tools/
  (test_repo_layout_guard.py), so a docs-only push skipped CI. The filters now
  include "*.md" and "tools/**".

Evidence: verification/2026-11-12-v14/ (gates, campaign, player-text audits,
offline and live probes, preview smoke, and the GitHub Actions run).
