+### 9.7 Sixth delivery (2026-11-12): `NovaAPI-v14` — the layout arrived correct and CI ran green
+
+The project was uploaded to a new repository, **`AbdElrhmanAhmed7/NovaAPI-v14`**
+(commit `24dc3e6`, message `v14`, 203 tracked files). For the first time in six
+deliveries the tree arrived **at the repository root**:
+
+```
+<git root>/
+├── .github/workflows/backend.yml   ← GitHub read it
+├── NOVA/backend/…
+├── README.md · PROJECT_STATUS.md · MIGRATION.md
+└── tools/ · verification/ · releases/ · reference/
+```
+
+The layout gate passed on the fresh clone, with no migration needed:
+
+```
+$ bash tools/check_layout.sh
+✓ layout ok – git root = project root, GitHub will run .github/workflows/backend.yml
+```
+
+**And GitHub agreed.** The `backend` workflow is `active` and ran on the push —
+3 jobs, 3 successes (`lint · types · content · contract`, `pytest (offline)`,
+`full campaign playthrough`). After five wrappers that produced *no CI at all*,
+this is the first delivery whose gates actually executed on GitHub:
+run [43252213875](https://github.com/AbdElrhmanAhmed7/NovaAPI-v14/actions/runs/43252213875),
+recorded in `verification/2026-11-12-v14/github-actions.json` / `.log`.
+
+Everything was then re-verified from scratch in a clean environment (new clone,
+new virtualenv), so the claim rests on this tree and not on the previous one:
+
+| Gate | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `check_layout.sh` | ✓ layout ok |
+| `ruff check .` | ✅ All checks passed |
+| `ruff format --check .` | ✅ 113 files already formatted |
+| `mypy app scripts` | ✅ no issues in 82 source files |
+| `validate_content.py --strict` | ✅ 15 missions / 95 actions – 0 errors, 0 warnings |
+| `audit_routes.py --check` | ✅ 0 errors, 0 warnings (67 operations, 15 guarded) |
+| `export_openapi.py --check` | ✅ contract up to date (67 operations) |
+| `pytest --cov=app` | ✅ **451 passed** · TOTAL **94%** (207.02 s) |
+| `playthrough.py --in-process --seed 7` | ✅ 15/15 · 93 ok / 0 mistakes · readiness 100 (S) · 259.5 s |
+| `audit_player_text.py` (in-process) | ✅ 996 responses · 56,445 strings · 473 distinct · 67/67 operations |
+| `live_probes.py --no-live` | ✅ 12 probes · 0 failures |
+| `live_probes.py` (live NASA) | ✅ **14 probes · 0 failures** · POWER `live` (Δmean 0.8858 °C, 4.06%) · POWER `cache` · APOD `bundled` |
+| `audit_player_text.py --base-url …` (real socket) | ✅ 996 responses · 56,562 strings · 476 distinct · 67/67 operations |
+| `preview_smoke.py --base-url …` | ✅ readiness · console 47,278 bytes / 0 external assets · repair-before-valve → 409 · correct order completes · 27 events |
+
+Same interpreter and libraries as the previous pass — Python 3.11.2, FastAPI 0.162.5,
+Pydantic 2.14.3, SQLAlchemy 2.0.57, uvicorn 0.54.0, pytest 9.2.0, ruff 0.17.4,
+mypy 2.4.1 — so the two runs are directly comparable. The single suite warning is
+still Starlette's own `httpx`/`TestClient` deprecation notice, not a project defect.
+
+**What was still unfinished when the previous session stopped**, and is now closed:
+
+1. **The delivery artefacts did not exist.** `releases/SHA256SUMS.txt` described a
+   patch and a zip that were not in the tree. Both are now regenerated from the
+   committed tree with `tools/make_release.sh --base 24dc3e6`, so the hashes, the
+   patch and the snapshot match one commit again.
+2. **The delivery documents pointed at the retired repository.** `releases/README.md`,
+   §13 below and `MIGRATION.md` still described `AbdElrhmanAhmed7/Final` and baseline
+   `11cefe5`. The current pointers now name `NovaAPI-v14` and `24dc3e6`; the earlier
+   sections (§9.1–§9.6, `MIGRATION.md` §1–§9) are kept unchanged as history.
+3. **A docs-only push skipped CI.** The workflow filters covered `NOVA/backend/**`
+   and the workflow file only, yet `test_project_docs.py` and
+   `test_repo_layout_guard.py` assert the root documents and `tools/`. The filters now
+   include `*.md` and `tools/**`, so a broken doc link can no longer land unverified.
+
+Evidence: `verification/2026-11-12-v14/` — `gates.log` (10 gates), `campaign.json`,
+`player-text.json` / `.md`, `player-text-live.json` / `.md` / `.log`,
+`live-probes.json` (offline), `live-probes-live.json` / `.log` (NASA POWER `live`),
+`preview-smoke.log`, and `github-actions.json` / `.log` (the green CI run on GitHub).
